RemoteFM14Move's changes to RemoteFM1's web/site (third_party/RemoteFM1, pinned), for the page the Ableton Move serves.
SPDX-License-Identifier: GPL-3.0-only (RemoteFM1's site, changed). Applied by scripts/build_site.sh (patch -p1 in the
copy of web/site), with web/move/js/*.js (host.js, movehost.js, moveui.js, moveslots.js, movemix.js, movebrowse.js, and
fw-browser.js: a copy of RemoteFM1's own, newer than the pinned site) and
web/move/css/move.css added beside it. Everything is behind one flag,
js/host.js ON_MOVE (index.html's <meta name="fm1-host" content="web|move">: the build sets "move"), so with "web" the
site is exactly RemoteFM1's: the patch can go upstream as it is (README.md, "The page").
  index.html     the flag; no http -> https redirect on the Move; <html data-host> for the CSS
  css/site.css   the header's install / app / FM-1 / recorder buttons hidden on the Move
  js/main.js     on the Move: the catalog is the Move's firmwares, the engine movehost.js (no AudioWorklet), no saves,
                 files, MIDI input, Use my FM-1, OMX-27, Move link, recorder, folder, audio input; the Editor talks to the
                 firmware on the Move (movehost.js midi(), moveEditors: remotefm1.com's editor list); the page follows the
                 firmware the Move switches to by itself; the Move's slots and Mix & FX (js/moveslots.js mountMoveUi:
                 the header's slot chips in place of the firmware picker, the phone's slot button, the Mix & FX view)
  js/editor-panel.js   on the Move: the engine "move" runs the firmware's own code; a hosted copy from remotefm1.com in
                 the live pages' sandbox (its own shim's tag dropped); a note for an editor that needs Web MIDI; no pop out
  js/sheet.js    on the Move: the firmware page is the Move's firmware browser (js/movebrowse.js sheetPage: the Move's
                 whole catalog as tiles, downloads); no saves, FM-1, playing, recording sections
  js/panel.js    a layout's buttons may name their legends' size (buttons.font; none of RemoteFM1's do): the Move's
                 phone layout sets 13 px, OCT 15 px (js/moveslots.js), as RemoteFM1 for iOS draws them

